From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 14:05:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): do not run the renderer's frame update on the
 UI thread (KD-19)

A v0.2.7 pane crashed reading a freed heap block in rebuildRow, iterating
a row's highlight list, reached from SetPreedit -> render_now on the XAML
UI thread by way of TSF's unfocus. The dump named every frame: 463
threads, 14 renderer/io pairs, and exactly one renderer thread not in its
event loop - parked on a renderer futex while the UI thread held the draw
mutex inside rebuildCells.

Upstream calls updateFrame from the surface's render thread and nowhere
else, and relies on it: the block that clears and repopulates every row's
highlight list, and the denormalization that resizes row_data, both run
outside any lock a second caller would take. Calling it from here was
never safe, whatever the export's comment claimed.

Nothing replaces the six calls. Each operation already queues a render
inside libghostty - selection through cursorPosCallback and
mouseButtonCallback, select_all and clear_selection in their binding
actions, preedit on all three of its paths, the scroll actions through
the IO thread - and the render thread renders immediately on that wakeup.

Verified in a pane, driving a real left-button drag with SendInput and
capturing the frame that follows it with no other input: 4404 selection
pixels on the dragged row in the ghostty pane, 5933 in the cascadia pane
beside it. Six focus round-trips over the path that crashed leave the
process alive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp    | 36 ++++++++++++-------
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.h      |  1 -
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
index 0c2812fb7..6c0a9f803 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
@@ -1142,13 +1142,29 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
     // is reached through a *named binding action* instead - the same route
     // ghostty's own keybindings take. `scroll_to_row` in Phase 5 was the first;
     // selection, search and copy in Phase 6 all arrive the same way.
-    void GhosttyControlCore::_renderNow() const
-    {
-        if (_surface)
-        {
-            ghostty_surface_render_now(_surface);
-        }
-    }
+    // There is no _renderNow, and that is deliberate - see KD-19.
+    //
+    // It used to call ghostty_surface_render_now, which ran the renderer's
+    // whole frame update on *this* thread. That is not a thing a second thread
+    // may do: upstream calls updateFrame from the surface's render thread and
+    // nowhere else, and the parts of it that clear and repopulate each row's
+    // highlight list, and that resize row_data, run outside any lock another
+    // caller would take. A ghostty pane crashed on 2026-08-18 reading a freed
+    // highlight list, with the UI thread inside rebuildCells and that surface's
+    // render thread parked on a renderer futex.
+    //
+    // Nothing replaces it, because nothing needs to: every operation these call
+    // sites perform already calls queueRender inside libghostty - selection
+    // through cursorPosCallback and mouseButtonCallback, select_all and
+    // clear_selection in their binding actions, preedit on all three of its
+    // paths, and the scroll actions through the IO thread. The render thread
+    // renders immediately on that wakeup; its coalescing timer is commented out
+    // upstream.
+    //
+    // The staleness this was written to fix was never coalescing either. It was
+    // the renderer wakeup being held by value, so notify() set a bool nobody
+    // read - ghostty patch 34, after which output alone drove 321 renders in
+    // the second where it used to manage 2.
 
     bool GhosttyControlCore::_bindingAction(const std::string_view action) const
     {
@@ -1294,7 +1310,6 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
     {
         // Only meaningful mid-drag, which is the only time WT calls it.
         _mouseTo(positionCore, _selectionMods());
-        _renderNow();
     }
 
     // The click that begins a selection.
@@ -1351,7 +1366,6 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
             _mouseDown = true;
         }
 
-        _renderNow();
 
         // Cascadia's meaning, not "is copy-on-select on": the flag says whether
         // there is now a selection worth copying when the button comes up. A
@@ -1404,14 +1418,12 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         }
         _releaseMouseIfHeld();
         _bindingAction("clear_selection");
-        _renderNow();
     }
 
     void GhosttyControlCore::SelectAll()
     {
         _releaseMouseIfHeld();
         _bindingAction("select_all");
-        _renderNow();
     }
 
     // Copy goes through ghostty rather than through read-back, because the
@@ -1685,7 +1697,6 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
             _bindingAction("scroll_to_bottom");
             break;
         }
-        _renderNow();
     }
     void GhosttyControlCore::SelectCommand(const bool /*goUp*/) {}
     void GhosttyControlCore::SelectOutput(const bool /*goUp*/) {}
@@ -1776,7 +1787,6 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         GhosttyEngine::RunWithEngineStack([&]() {
             ghostty_surface_preedit(_surface, utf8.data(), utf8.size());
         });
-        _renderNow();
     }
     bool GhosttyControlCore::ForceCursorVisible() const noexcept { return false; }
     void GhosttyControlCore::ForceCursorVisible(bool /*force*/) {}
diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.h b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.h
index c1ac2d434..e2bf66c79 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.h
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.h
@@ -275,7 +275,6 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
 
         // Output has to draw itself; libghostty's wakeup coalesces. Same
         // reasoning as _connectionOutputHandler's render.
-        void _renderNow() const;
         void _raiseSwapChainChanged();
         void _raiseOnUiThread(std::function<void()> action);
 
